actions involving publicly traded domestic freight railroad companies that shared\n1724: certain characteristics with the merger. Based on publicly available information, BMO identified nine publicly announced and completed transactions involving domestic companies that owned and operated freight railroad companies occurring since\n1725: January 1, 2005. BMO analyzed EV to LTM EBITDA (for the 12-month period prior to the public announcement of each respective transaction) for each of these transactions for comparison purposes. The selected transactions and corresponding data were as\n1726: follows:\n1727: Selected Precedent Transactions\n1728: Announcement Date\n1729: Acquiror\n1730: Target\n1731: February 2015\n1732: Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n1733: Freightliner Group\n1734: July 2012\n1735: Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n1736: RailAmerica, Inc.\n1737: November 2009\n1738: Berkshire Hathaway, Inc.\n1739: Burlington Northern Santa Fe Corporation\n1740: January 2008\n1741: Canadian National Railway Co.\n1742: EJ & E Railway, Co.\n1743: August 2008\n1744: Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n1745: Ohio Central Railway System\n1746: September 2007\n1747: Canadian Pacific Railway, Ltd.\n1748: Dakota, Minnesota & Eastern Railroad, Corp.\n1749: November 2006\n1750: Fortress Investment Group\n1751: RailAmerica, Inc.\n1752: September 2005\n1753: RailAmerica, Inc.\n1754: Alcoa Railroad Operations\n1755: May 2005\n1756: Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n1757: Rail Management Corporation’s rail operations\n1758: For purposes of this analysis, BMO derived a range of multiples for each metric using the high and low\n1759: multiples from the selected precedent transactions. For informational purposes only, and not relied upon in reaching any conclusions, BMO also reviewed the mean and median multiples from the selected precedent transactions.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1760]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 160, \"offset\": 16