{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824418986,"sessionID":"ses_f4629b1bbffezZEiat5kIdVPT6","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d9440c0016ml3G4gbWB2i6F","sessionID":"ses_f4629b1bbffezZEiat5kIdVPT6","messageID":"msg_0b9d93c2f001MLht7wdNAfCXt5","type":"tool","id":"call_00_vLbAyHSuzR2M5sj3RB2e0647","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":140,"offset":2820,"path":"/tmp/opencode/filing_lines.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_lines.txt, lines 2820-2959\n2820: Failure to comply strictly with all of the procedures set forth in Section 7-1.2-1202 of the RIBCA will result in the loss of a\n2821: shareholder’s statutory dissenters’ rights.\n2822: 70\n2823: Table of Contents\n2824: MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK\n2825: Our common stock is quoted on the NASDAQ under the trading symbol “PWX”. The following table sets forth, for the periods indicated,\n2826: the high and low sale prices per share for our common stock as reported on the NASDAQ. Our preferred stock is not quoted on a market and is non-cumulative and the dividend is limited to $5.00 per share per annum and is convertible to 100 shares of\n2827: common stock. Also included are dividends paid per share of common stock and preferred stock during these quarterly periods.\n2828: Common Stock\n2829: Trading Prices\n2830: Dividends Paid\n2831: High\n2832: Low\n2833: Preferred\n2834: Common\n2835: 2014\n2836: First Quarter\n2837: $\n2838: 19.95\n2839: $\n2840: 17.00\n2841: $\n2842: 5.00\n2843: $\n2844: 0.04\n2845: Second Quarter\n2846: 19.45\n2847: 17.30\n2848: –0–\n2849: 0.04\n2850: Third Quarter\n2851: 18.50\n2852: 17.04\n2853: –0–\n2854: 0.04\n2855: Fourth Quarter\n2856: 20.00\n2857: 16.70\n2858: –0–\n2859: 0.04\n2860: 2015\n2861: First Quarter\n2862: $\n2863: 19.64\n2864: $\n2865: 17.60\n2866: $\n2867: 5.00\n2868: $\n2869: 0.04\n2870: Second Quarter\n2871: 18.97\n2872: 17.25\n2873: –0–\n2874: 0.04\n2875: Third Quarter\n2876: 17.75\n2877: 15.20\n2878: –0–\n2879: 0.04\n2880: Fourth Quarter\n2881: 16.25\n2882: 13.05\n2883: –0–\n2884: 0.04\n2885: 2016\n2886: First Quarter\n2887: $\n2888: 15.82\n2889: $\n2890: 12.50\n2891: $\n2892: 5.00\n2893: $\n2894: 0.04\n2895: Second Quarter\n2896: 17.64\n2897: 14.12\n2898: –0–\n2899: 0.04\n2900: Third Quarter (through September 16, 2016)\n2901: 25.00\n2902: 15.60\n2903: –0–\n2904: 0.04\n2905: As of September 16, 2016, there were 4,866,593 shares of common stock outstanding, held by\n2906: approximately 540 holders of record of common stock and 640 shares of preferred stock outstanding, held by 8 holders of record of preferred stock.\n2907: The declaration of cash dividends on both the common stock and the preferred stock is made at the discretion of the Board based on the\n2908: Company’s earnings, financial condition, capital requirements and other relevant factors and restrictions. Under the merger agreement, described in “The Merger Agreement—Conduct of Business Pending the Merger,” the Company is\n2909: prohibited from paying any dividend or other distribution on Company stock (other than regular quarterly dividends on common stock not in excess of $0.04 per share and the regular annual dividend on preferred stock not in excess of $5.00 per share,\n2910: in each case consistent with past practice).\n2911: 71\n2912: Table of Contents\n2913: THE VOTING AGREEMENT\n2914: The following summary of the voting agreement is qualified by reference to the complete text of the voting agreement, which is attached to\n2915: this proxy statement as\n2916: Annex B\n2917: and incorporated into this proxy statement by reference.\n2918: In connection with the execution of the\n2919: merger agreement, G&W and the Company entered into a voting agreement with the Robert H. Eder Trust and the Linda Eder Trust (which we refer to as the “Eder Trusts”), which, as of the date of the voting agreement, collectively owned\n2920: 842,742 shares of common stock and 500 shares of preferred stock. Under the voting agreement, each Eder Trust must vote all of its shares of Company stock:\n2921: •\n2922: in favor of approval of the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated by the merger agreement, including the merger and any other action reasonably requested by G&W in furtherance thereof;\n2923: •\n2924: against any other merger agreement, merger, consolidation, combination, sale of substantial assets, reorganization, recapitalization, dissolution, liquidation or winding up of or by the Company;\n2925: •\n2926: against any takeover proposal; and\n2927: •\n2928: against any amendment of the Company’s articles of incorporation or bylaws or any other action, proposal agreement or transaction involving the Company or any of its subsidiaries which could reasonably be expected\n2929: to in any manner impede, frustrate, prevent, adversely affect, interfere with or nullify any provision of the merger agreement, the plan of merger attached thereto or any other transaction documents (including the voting agreement), the merger or\n2930: any related transaction or change in any manner the voting rights of any capital stock of the Company.\n2931: Under the voting\n2932: agreement, each of the Eder Trusts agreed not to, and not to permit any of its representatives, to:\n2933: •\n2934: solicit, initiate, encourage or take any other action to facilitate any inquiries with respect to a potential takeover proposal or action which would impede, frustrate, prevent, adversely affect, interfere with or\n2935: nullify any provision of the merger agreement, the plan of merger attached thereto, any other transaction document (including the voting agreement), the merger or any related transaction or change in any manner the voting rights of any capital stock\n2936: of the Company;\n2937: •\n2938: enter into any agreement, or provide any person any information with respect to, any takeover proposal or any action which would impede, frustrate, prevent adversely affect, interfere with or nullify any provision of\n2939: the merger agreement, the plan of merger attached thereto, any other transaction document (including the voting agreement), the merger or any related transaction or change in any manner the voting rights of any capital stock of the Company;\n2940: •\n2941: enter into, continue or otherwise participate in any discussions or negotiations regarding, or furnish to any person any information with respect to, the Company, a takeover proposal or any action which would impede,\n2942: frustrate, prevent adversely affect, interfere with or nullify any provision of the merger agreement, the plan of merger attached thereto, any other transaction document (including the voting agreement), the merger or any related transaction or\n2943: change in any manner the voting rights of any capital stock of the Company, or take any other action to facilitate any inquiries or the making of any proposal that constitutes or is reasonably likely to lead to any takeover proposal or an action\n2944: which would impede, frustrate, prevent, adversely affect, interfere with or nullify any provision of the merger agreement, the plan of merger attached thereto, any other transaction document (including the voting agreement), the merger or any\n2945: related transaction or change in any manner the voting rights of any capital stock of the Company;\n2946: •\n2947: approve, endorse or recommend any proposal that constitutes, or is reasonably expected to lead to, a takeover proposal; or\n2948: •\n2949: authorize or commit to do any of the foregoing.\n2950: 72\n2951: Table of Contents\n2952: In addition, except under limited circumstances, the Eder Trusts also agreed not to sell, assign,\n2953: transfer or otherwise dispose of or encumber their shares of Company stock while the voting agreement is in effect. The Eder Trusts also agreed to waive and not exercise or assent to any dissenters’ rights under the RIBCA in connection with the\n2954: merger or to commence or participate in any claim against the Company, G&W or any of their respective successors relating to the negotiation, execution and delivery of the voting agreement or the merger agreement or the consummation of the\n2955: merger or any related transactions (other than claims to the extent relating to or based upon any alleged breach by G&W of the voting agreement). The voting agreement terminates immediately upon the earlier of the effective time of the merger,\n2956: the termination of the merger agreement in accordance with its terms, or mutual written agreement of G&W and the Eder Trusts.\n2957: 73\n2958: Table of Contents\n2959: MATERIAL UNITED STATES FEDERAL INCOME TAX CONSEQUENCES OF THE MERGER\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2960]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_lines.txt, lines 2820-2959\n2820: Failure to comply strictly with all of the procedures set forth in Section 7-1.2-1202 of the RIBCA will result in the loss of a\n2821: shareholder’s statutory dissenters’ rights.\n2822: 70\n2823: Table of Contents\n2824: MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK\n2825: Our common stock is quoted on the NASDAQ under the trading symbol “PWX”. The following table sets forth, for the periods indicated,\n2826: the high and low sale prices per share for our common stock as reported on the NASDAQ. Our preferred stock is not quoted on a market and is non-cumulative and the dividend is limited to $5.00 per share per annum and is convertible to 100 shares of\n2827: common stock. Also included are dividends paid per share of common stock and preferred stock during these quarterly periods.\n2828: Common Stock\n2829: Trading Prices\n2830: Dividends Paid\n2831: High\n2832: Low\n2833: Preferred\n2834: Common\n2835: 2014\n2836: First Quarter\n2837: $\n2838: 19.95\n2839: $\n2840: 17.00\n2841: $\n2842: 5.00\n2843: $\n2844: 0.04\n2845: Second Quarter\n2846: 19.45\n2847: 17.30\n2848: –0–\n2849: 0.04\n2850: Third Quarter\n2851: 18.50\n2852: 17.04\n2853