a=True)\n r = S(r, 'Named bidders', 'Party A \\u2014 Strategic (Class I rail partner); unpriced Q4 2015 approach; last named April 2016; closed by Count-0 identity row R042 (Inferred: identity). G&W \\u2014 Strategic; winner; bids R035, R036, R052; signed R056 (no exit row). Party B \\u2014 Strategic; $24.00 LOI R028 and late reaffirmation R050; Not selected at signing R053 (Would not improve earlier offer). Party C \\u2014 Strategic late entrant; IOI $21.00 R025, LOI $19.30 R031; Dropped R038. Party D \\u2014 Financial; LOI $21.00 R030, revised $24.00 R045; paused R048; closed by inferred R054. Party E \\u2014 Strategic; LOI $21.26 R029, revised $23.81 with Party F support R046, reverted to $21.26 R047; closed by inferred R055. Party F \\u2014 Strategic; LOI $19.20 R032; Dropped R041; later gave financing support to E (no membership change).')\n r = S(r, 'Cohorts (not extra parties)', '11 strategic NDA signers (R009); 14 financial NDA signers (R010); nine IOI bidders, type Unknown (R018); two excluded low bidders, Unknown (R020); 16 non-submitting signers, Unknown (R019); two non-submitting LOI bidders, split strategic/financial (R033\\u2013R034). Two additional Class I railroads were contacted but never entered (R013).')\n r = S(r, 'Ownership / country attributes', 'PWRR is US (Rhode Island); G&W is US (Delaware). Eder Trusts hold 842,742 common shares (17.3%) and 500 preferred (78.1%); directors/officers hold ~22.7% of common and ~78.1% of preferred (X-013, p.72). Director Alfred P. Smith (GATX VP; GATX owns 4.92% of common) recused from the process (P-023, p.30).')\n-r = S(r, 'Advisers', 'GHF / BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\u2014 Company financial adviser; GHF engaged 01/27/2016 (R002); BMO acquired GHF\\u2019s business 08/01/2016 (one continuing relationship); fee ~$2.52 million; BMO affiliate ~5% lender in G&W\\u2019s syndicated facility, reviewed 09/06/2016 (R058). Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP \\u2014 Company legal counsel (first observed 03/24/2016, R005). Sim