evidence.\n  [5] R001, R015, R024–R026, R029–R037, R043 (Type; identity descriptions)\n  [6] Reassigning any type would change Summary participant lines and could affect cohort splits; naming anonymous parties from outside knowledge is out of scope by instruction.\n  [7] Pending\n---- row 6\n  [1] Q5\n  [2] Inferred/closing outcomes and their agency (every inferred row grouped by transition)\n  [3] Accept the closures: R020 (Did not submit, Inferred: residual — 25 − 9 = 16, working 05/19) and R034/R035 (stated non-submissions, by 07/20); R043 (Party A, Inferred: identity, Count 0, first named set excluding it 07/27); R056/R057 (D and E, Inferred: silent at the 08/12 signing). D’s 08/02 statement is treated as Participation paused, not an exit.\n  [4] Bases and arithmetic are in section 10.2 of the instruction and each row’s Why cell: R020 uses the 25-signer base and nine submitters (P-006, p.28; P-011, p.29); R043 uses the 07/27 continuation of “G&W and Party B” (P-023, p.30); D/E last appear 08/02 and the next identified transition is signing (P-024, p.30; P-033, p.32). The filing does not state who the two lowest IOIs were or which anonymous\n  [5] R020, R021, R034, R035, R043, R049, R056, R057 (Outcome basis; Count; Decided by; Exit reason)\n  [6] If the 25-signer base or the nine-submitter set is corrected, R020’s Count and the Round 1 balance change; if Party A is instead mapped to a named exit, only R043’s covering-row list changes — counts must not move to the name.\n  [7] Pending\n---- row 7\n  [1] Q6\n  [2] Formality and conditions borderline calls (including the late reconfirmation and every diligence-period Heavy)\n  [3] Keep: nine-IOI cohort Informal/Heavy by context (R019); Party C IOI Informal/Heavy (R026); B’s LOI and reaffirmation Formal/Light with “DD required: confirmatory” mapping an expedited diligence review (R029, R051; R051 is a flagged late reconfirmation — Reaffirmed by: returned draft, $24 carried forward); E’s LOIs/reversion Informal/Heavy with the 60-day exclusivity (R030, R047, R048); D Formal/He\n  [4] Formal signals: B, G&W and D returned agreement mark-ups (P-015, p.29); E provided only an issues summary (P-015); the final G&W bid carried mark-ups and was priced during definitive negotiation (P-028, p.31). Heavy triggers are stated multi-week/exclusive diligence periods (P-016–P-021, p.29–30; P-024, p.30). B’s reaffirmation meets the three-part late-reconfirmation test (P-026/P-027, p.31).\n  [5] R019, R026, R029–R037, R046–R051, R054 (Formality; Conditions level; Conditions detail; Price origin)\n  [6] A reviewer treating E’s issues summary as a returned markup would make E Formal; treating B’s expedited review as substantive would make B Heavy; either change alters the deal-history reading but not the outcome.\n  [7] Pending\n---- row 8\n  [1] Q7\n  [2] Working-date conventions that decide row order (05/19 IOI window, mid-June, early-July Party C, the five undated LOIs vs G&W 07/21, deadline-revision window, 07/29 re-entries)\n  [3] Keep the assigned Working dates and the disclosed methods: R019 05/19 (Assigned: deadline); R023 06/15 (midpoint of 06/11–19); R024/R025 07/05 (midpoint of 07/01–10; R025 Assigned: sequence); R029–R033 07/20 (Assigned: deadline) displayed before G&W’s 07/21 exact LOI — their relative order is not known and is a display convention only; R017 05/08 (midpoint of the derived 04/28–05/18 window); R039–\n  [4] The instruction’s date rules and the filing’s own sequencing (P-010, P-012, P-014–P-017, P-023). Example: the five undated LOIs cannot be shown to have arrived before G&W’s 07/21 LOI or after their 07/20 deadline; the ledger sorts them at the deadline and says so (R029–R033).\n  [5] R017, R019, R023–R035, R039–R045 (Working date; Date basis; Date method; # order)\n  [6] Moving any assigned date within its own window would change # order and possibly stage counts; reported and inferred dates are not moved.\n  [7] Pending\n---- row 9\n  [1] Q8\n  [2] Post-signing matters, contingent consideration and comparability inputs\n  [3] Keep the 09/06/2016 BMO conflict row as a Material process update (R060); keep the CVR ($1.13/share, South Quay) only in G&W’s July bid rows and the Summary; keep the preferred 100-for-1 conversion and the labelled $2,500 per preferred share conversion in the Summary; no go-shop and no observed post-signing competing proposal.\n  [4] Background p.32 (P-034) and the financial-analysis Miscellaneous section (X-006/X-007, p.41–42: ~5% affiliate participation; $1–5 million revenue since 01/01/2014). CVR defined in P-017, p.29. Consideration X-008, p.50. No go-shop provision appears in the merger-agreement summaries reviewed.\n  [5] R036, R037, R054, R058, R060 (Terms; All cash; Cash at closing; Summary comparability)\n  [6] Treating the CVR as non-cash or ignoring the BMO relationship would misstate G&W’s July consideration or the adviser-conflict record; the preferred conversion changes only the Summary conversion, not per-common-share bids.\n  [7] Pending\n---- row 11\n  [1] SECTION 13 CHECK RESULTS (run on this delivered version)\n---- row 12\n  [1] 1. Coverage and materiality\n  [2] Passed with qualifications\n  [3] All disclosed core offers, contacts/NDAs, selections, outcomes, deadlines, signing and publicity are represented (R001–R060). Qualifications: no go-shop exists and no post-signing competition is reported, so none appears; contact-only parties (two Class I railroads) and never-admitted parties have no outcome rows by convention. Routine meetings were folded into related rows.\n---- row 13\n  [1] 2. Counts and population\n  [2] Qualified\n  [3] Ledger formulas: contacts 33 units; NDA signers 26 events; round-bidder tallies 9 / 6 / 4. Filing assertions retained: 11+18 contacted; 25 NDA signers; nine IOIs; six LOIs. Unresolved: 25 vs 26 signer reconciliation (Q3) and Party B’s blank contact Count. Per-stage balance shown in Summary section 5; alternative counts are qualified rather than forced.\n---- row 14\n  [1] 3. Participation continuity\n  [2] Passed with qualifications\n  [3] Every entered participant ends in a stated outcome, an inferred closing row, or signing; re-entries recorded for D/E (R044–R045). Qualifications: Party A’s exit is a Count-0 identity row (Q5), and the two non-submitting LOI bidders and 16 non-submitters are anonymous residuals. Stock per stage: R1 25−16−2=7; R2 8−2−4=2; R3 2+2−3=1 (winner).\n---- row 15\n  [1] 4. Dates and order\n  [2] Passed (programmatic)\n  [3] Sorting by Working date then # reproduces # order (verified by code); no Working date falls outside its own Date from/to; Reported/Inferred labels match Date basis; deadline communication, deadlines and signing are distinct. Application-level date checking (Excel recalculation) not performed.\n---- row 16\n  [1] 5. Offers and classifications\n  [2] Passed with qualifications\n  [3] Every Bid and Bid reaffirmed row has Formality, Conditions level and a fixed-format Conditions detail string (verified by code); price kinds/origins, currencies and cash flags agree with the text; signing, reaffirmations, reversions and group envelope are not counted as separate priced submissions. Qualifications: Q6 borderline calls (E’s issues-summary formality; mapping expedited review to confi\n---- row 17\n  [1] 6. Structure and consistency\n  [2] Passed (programmatic)\n  [3] Each numbered round has exactly one Round opened row (R007, R022, R038) with a Round finality value; R007 carries the R1 anchor tag with rejected candidates; every Deadline row has a treatment matching the Summary map; every inferred row opens with its Outcome basis; Page is filled wherever Source is; Date basis/Date method pairs are permitted.\n---- row 18\n  [1] 7. Evidence\n  [2] Passed with declared normalization\n  [3] Every quotation in Why and evidence was checked programmatically as an exact substring of its cited Source text paragraph (curly quotes and whitespace normalized only at layout level). Interpretation over and above the quotations (rounds, conventions, agency) is argued in the cells and Questions. Text matching alone is not proof of interpretation.\n---- row 19\n  [1] 8. Review and workbook operation\n  [2] Qualified\n  [3] Question links and affected rows resolve to defined Row ids; validations reference the Lists sheet; AI original matches the ledger baseline (row-by-row value comparison by Row id performed); conditional formatting highlights changes by Row id/column. Not performed in Excel: formula recalculation, drop-down and hyperlink behavior, and print/layout inspection; a LibreOffice open/save smoke test was \n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\\nws = wb['Questions']\\nfor r in range(1, ws.max_row+1):\\n    vals = [ws.cell(row=r, column=c).value for c in range(1, 9)]\\n    if any(vals):\\n        print('---- row', r)\\n        for c, v in enumerate(vals, 1):\\n            if v: print(f'  [{c}] {str(v)[:400]}')\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825119058,"end":1789825119815}}}}
