{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825130904,"sessionID":"ses_f4629b1bbffezZEiat5kIdVPT6","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e41a300014cgeRFZcCepf1d","sessionID":"ses_f4629b1bbffezZEiat5kIdVPT6","messageID":"msg_0b9e3f65c001NbzpCVJc88s7ZE","type":"tool","id":"call_01_zPXKmhg5EsUEvGceDReg8366","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 build_workbook.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\nhdr = [c.value for c in ws[1]]\nci = {h:i+1 for i,h in enumerate(hdr)}\nrows = [{h: ws.cell(row=r, column=ci[h]).value for h in hdr} for r in range(2, ws.max_row+1)]\nfor rid in ['R007','R008','R009','R010','R012','R014','R020','R021','R044','R045','R047','R048','R055']:\n    d = next(x for x in rows if x['Row id']==rid)\n    print('====', rid, d['What happened'], '|', d['When'])\n    print('  terms:', (d['Terms or outcome'] or '')[:260])\n    print('  related:', d['Related rows'])\n# source sheet\nsrc = wb['Source text']\nprint('source rows:', src.max_row-1)\nids = [src.cell(row=r, column=1).value for r in range(2, src.max_row+1)]\nprint('first/last:', ids[0], ids[-1], 'x rows:', len([i for i in ids if i.startswith('X')]))\n# continuation markers\nfor r in range(2, src.max_row+1):\n    if 'continuation' in (src.cell(row=r, column=2).value or ''):\n        print('cont:', ids[r-2], src.cell(row=r, column=1).value, src.cell(row=r, column=2).value)\nEOF"},"output":"ledger rows after adviser insertion: 60 ids R001.. R060\nsaved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx rows 60\n==== R007 Round opened | Week of 03/28/2016\n  terms: R1 anchor: first outreach wave (week of 03/28/2016) — GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) and 18 potential financial buyers (29 total). Other candidate anchors rejected: R005 (03/24/2016 Transaction Committee authorization — rejecte\n  related: R003; R005 (candidate anchors)\n==== R008 Contact | Week of 03/28/2016\n  terms: Outreach to determine interest in a change in control transaction; all 11 subsequently executed confidentiality agreements (R010). Count 11 — size of the disclosed strategic cohort.\n  related: R010 (NDA cohort)\n==== R009 Contact | Week of 03/28/2016\n  terms: Outreach to determine interest; 14 of the 18 subsequently executed confidentiality agreements (R011). Count 18 contacted (not the 14 signers).\n  related: R011 (NDA cohort)\n==== R010 NDA signed | After the week of 03/28/2016; exact dates not disclosed\n  terms: Executed acquisition-related confidentiality agreements; no “standstill” or similar provision restricting proposals. Signers received the Company memorandum in late April 2016 (folded here; no separate row per section 4). Includes Party A, G&W and (by the fili\n  related: R008 (contacts); R015 (Party B); R043 (Party A)\n==== R012 Contact | 04/03/2016–04/06/2016\n  terms: Series of introductory meetings at the 2016 Connections Convention. Count 0 — these five are inside the R008 11-strategic cohort; first reported event naming G&W.\n  related: covered by R008\n==== R014 Contact | On or before 04/07/2016 (report date; earlier contacts not dated)\n  terms: Target-side approaches to determine interest in a possible transaction; additional to the 11 strategic buyers contacted in the March wave. No NDA, bid or outcome is reported: these contact-only parties never entered the process (no closing row).\n  related: None\n==== R020 Did not submit | By 05/19/2016\n  terms: Inferred: residual — 25 NDA signers (R010+R011) − 9 IOI submitters (R019) = 16 non-submitters. Base assumes all 25 initial signers were eligible for the IOI solicitation (P-010, p.29); may include Party A (see R043).\n  related: R010; R011; R043 (possible member)\n==== R021 Dropped by target | 06/01/2016 (decision reached over the 05/23 and 06/01 meetings)\n  terms: Stated exclusion from management presentations and further diligence because management time for presentations was substantial; the two lowest of the nine IOIs. Stage left: Round 1. Identity of the two lowest is not disclosed.\n  related: R019 (source group); R043 (possible member)\n==== R044 Re-entered | 07/29/2016\n  terms: GHF calls; D expressed interest in reengaging and enhancing its offer — renewed participation after the 07/27/2016 drop (see R040); revised LOI followed on 08/01/2016.\n  related: R040; R046\n==== R045 Re-entered | 07/29/2016\n  terms: GHF calls; E expressed interest in reengaging and enhancing its offer — renewed participation after the 07/27/2016 drop (see R041); revised LOI followed on 08/01/2016.\n  related: R041; R047\n==== R047 Bid | 08/01/2016\n  terms: Support: Party F (financing) — revised LOI at $23.81 per share with a 30-day due diligence period, submitted along with financing support from Party F. Related rows point to Party F’s earlier independent bid (R033); F had already exited on 07/27/2016 (R042), s\n  related: revises R030; R033 (Party F prior bid); R045; R048\n==== R048 Bid | 08/02/2016\n  terms: Bid reversion — withdrew its revised $23.81 proposal and confirmed its original $21.26 per-share proposal (with its 60-day exclusivity condition). A withdrawal of the higher proposal while confirming the older one is a reversion, not a process withdrawal.\n  related: withdraws R047; reverts to R030; closed by R057\n==== R055 Not selected at signing | 08/12/2016\n  terms: Still bidding when the Board chose G&W: at the Board’s request BMO asked Party B whether it would increase its price and Party B declined. Exit reason: Would not improve earlier offer (asked to improve and declined); agency remains with the target’s selection.\n  related: R051; R058\nsource rows: 50\nfirst/last: P-001 X-016 x rows: 16\ncont: P-004 P-004 Background of the Merger (continuation of previous paragraph)\ncont: P-010 P-010 Background of the Merger (continuation of previous paragraph)\ncont: P-026 P-026 Background of