{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825240799,"sessionID":"ses_f4629b1bbffezZEiat5kIdVPT6","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e5bac2001eUsXJYxSqbU6kU","sessionID":"ses_f4629b1bbffezZEiat5kIdVPT6","messageID":"msg_0b9e5b086001pAJaL5AGlGRFRQ","type":"text","text":"The workbook is delivered at `extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx` (named exactly as you asked; the instruction's default name would have been `providence-worcester_ledger.xlsx`). It has the four visible sheets — **Deal ledger** (60 rows, 14 visible columns + 11 collapsed expandable field groups), **Summary**, **Questions**, **Source text** (P-001–P-034 = complete background pp.27–32; X-001–X-016 = additional passages used) — plus hidden **AI original** (values-only baseline) and **Lists** (drop-downs). Status: **AI first pass; not human-approved** (instruction revision 19 Sep 2026).\n\n## The sale, in plain terms\n\nProvidence & Worcester's Q4 2015 meeting with a Class I rail partner (\"Party A\") produced an unpriced interest in acquiring equity. The board hired GHF (approved 01/27/2016), decided on 03/14/2016 to run a broad process, and GHF's week-of-03/28/2016 wave contacted 11 strategic and 18 financial buyers; 25 signed confidentiality agreements (no standstills), plus Party C in early July. Nine non-binding IOIs ($17.93–$26.50/share) arrived 05/19–06/01/2016; the two lowest were cut and seven advanced to management presentations and a July 20 LOI round. Six LOIs arrived in late July ($19.20–$24.00); on 07/27/2016 the committee picked **G&W** and **Party B** ($24.00) for confirmatory diligence and definitive negotiation, dropping Parties C, D, E and F. G&W's July bids carried a $1.13/share CVR tied to the South Quay property sale and asked for three-week exclusive diligence; it revised to $22.15 on 07/26. D and E re-engaged on 07/29–08/02 (D at $24.00, then paused; E at $23.81 with Party F financing support, then reverted to $21.26). On 08/12/2016, after B declined to improve, G&W bid **$25.00 all cash** (CVR dropped) with merger-agreement mark-ups and a 6:00 p.m. 08/13 expiry; the board approved and signed the same day, announcing 08/15/2016. **Observed outcome: signed merger agreement** (announced 08/15/2016); no go-shop, no post-signing competing proposal in the proxy; closing not observed (expected Q4 2016); preferred converts 100-for-1 into the same $25.00.\n\n## Most consequential review items (details on the Questions sheet)\n\n- **Q3 NDA reconciliation (25 vs 26):** I record 11 + 14 = 25 wave signers *plus* Party C = 26 signer events; the Reasons section says 25. Recommended: keep both and treat the difference as Party C. Changing this alters the Summary totals.\n- **Q2/PQ17 05/19 deadline:** I classified it **Enforced** (the 05/19–06/01 receipt window merely straddles the date; the target advanced on 06/01); a reviewer reading the later arrivals as accepted would switch it to **Late bids accepted**.\n- **Q5 inferred closures:** 16 non-submitters (25 − 9, at 05/19), Party A's Count-0 identity row (likely already inside that 16), and D/E closed as \"Not selected at signing\" (Inferred: silent); D's 08/02 statement is a pause, not an exit. Any base-population correction moves these counts.\n- **Q6 formality/conditions:** the nine-IOI cohort is Informal/Heavy by context; Party E's issues summary is Informal (a reviewer could call it a returned markup); Party B's expedited review is mapped to \"DD required: confirmatory\" (Light), and its 08/04 returned draft is a flagged late reconfirmation ($24 carried forward).\n- **Q1/Q7 round map and date conventions:** one process, rounds R0–R3 (R1 anchored on the outreach wave; R3 Inferred final); the five undated LOIs sort at the 07/20 deadline before G&W's exact 07/21 LOI as a display convention only.\n\n## Checks\n\nPassed programmatically: coverage of offers/contacts/outcomes/signing; quote fidelity (every quotation is an exact substring of its cited source paragraph); date order and method/basis pairs; per-stage balances (25−16−2=7; 8−2−4=2; 2+2−3=1); counts (contacts 33, NDAs 26, round tallies 9/6/4); AI original equals the ledger; 15 drop-down validations; no merged cells. **Qualified:** count reconciliation 25/26 and Party B's blank contact overlap; borderline formality/conditions calls. **Not run/unsupported:** spreadsheet-application testing (formula recalculation, drop-downs, hyperlinks) — LibreOffice is installed but crashes at startup here, so formulas and conditional-formatting logic were verified programmatically only; I have not opened the workbook in Excel.","time":{"start":1789825235650,"end":1789825240799}}}
